sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The foldings of the blastoderm that produce the neural and amniotic folds result from unequal rates of growth, local accelerations and retardations, in what is at first an even and uniform layer of embryonic tissue, in the way that a sheet buckles when parts of it expand or contract.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Embryonic folds arise from local differences in growth rate of a uniform sheet";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Embryology and unequal growth”. Scope: vertebrate embryos (blastoderm / germinal disc), especially the chick"
}
